{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KCr29KknKLvQXRoVk7bqHd","type":"tool_result","content":"0\t## 当前项目\n1\t当前绑定项目：**distill_sparse_swiglu**\n2\t\n3\t## 按需查阅\n4\t- 项目配置：`load_project_config(\"distill_sparse_swiglu\")` 或 `load_project_config(\"distill_sparse_swiglu\", section=\"execution\")`\n5\t- 知识文件：`read_project_file(file=...)` 读取项目文件（ROADMAP.md/memory.md/ideas.md/report.md 等）\n6\t- 路线图：`read_roadmap()` 读取研究方向和短期任务\n7\t- 产出目录：`/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_14/projects/distill_sparse_swiglu/artifacts/`（写文件后用 `register_artifact` 注册）\n8\t\n9\t## 用户自定义规则（必须遵守）\n10\t### 审稿规则\n11\t\n12\t- **[EMNLP 2026]** “EMNLP 2026 通过 ARR 统一审稿，Main/Findings 不分开投稿（不是两个Track），Long/Short 也走同一审稿系统，Overall Assessment的评分标准如下：5 = Consider for Award（约前2.5%），4.5 = Borderline Award，4 = Conference（可被主会议接收），3.5 = Borderline Conference，3 = Findings（可被Findings接收），2.5 = Borderline Findings，2 = Resubmit next cycle（需大幅修改，可在下一周期完成），1.5 = Resubmit after next cycle（需大幅修改，无法在下一周期完成），1 = Do not resubmit（需完全重做或与*ACL无关）”\n13\t\n14\t> 以上规则由用户配置，优先级等同于硬约束。违反会被 Reviewer 标记。\n15\t\n16\t## Worker 操作规范\n17\t\n18\t### paper-writing-norms\n19\t\n20\t# 论文写作风格规范\n21\t\n22\t> 核心哲学：**论文是一个有说服力的故事，不是实验报告。** 审稿人在几十秒内判断论文价值——如果 Abstract 和 Introduction 读起来像实验日志，论文就已经失败了。\n23\t\n24\t---\n25\t\n26\t## 一、总体写作哲学\n27\t\n28\t### 1.1 故事驱动，不是数据堆砌\n29\t\n30\t- 论文必须以\"故事线\"为核心展开：问题 → 洞察 → 方法 → 验证\n31\t- 禁止大量实验数据堆砌——每个数字出现必须服务于叙事推进\n32\t- 附录内容必须在正文中有明确引用且融入叙事，禁止简单堆砌\n33\t- 如果附录数据对核心叙事有重大影响，根据附录数据调整论文 framing\n34\t\n35\t### 1.2 主线统一性\n36\t\n37\t- 当 idea 在研究过程中发生变化后，**必须重审全文逻辑**\n38\t- 常见问题：Introduction 讲的故事 A，Method 做的是故事 B，Results 又在讲故事 C\n39\t- 修复方式：从最终实验结论反推，重写 Introduction 的问题定义和动机\n40\t- 每次 idea 调整后检查：Abstract → Introduction → Method → Results → Discussion → Conclusion 是否形成一条连贯主线\n41\t\n42\t### 1.3 专有名词必须有定义\n43\t\n44\t- 首次出现的专有名词/缩写必须给出完整定义和解释\n45\t- Abstract 中使用的缩写也必须在 Abstract 内定义（如 LLM = Large Language Model）\n46\t- 不能假设读者知道你自己定义的术语——论文从来没解释过的概念不能直接使用\n47\t- 通用规则：如果一个非标准术语第一次出现时没有括号定义，就是写作 bug\n48\t\n49\t### 1.4 写作前必读同类优秀论文"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"263fa585-9870-446a-8635-ded3c7ec2e0a","uuid":"36e558f4-9987-4ff5-8bd8-5d519c428878","timestamp":"2026-05-18T18:37:07.549Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_14/projects/distill_sparse_swiglu/.claude/CLAUDE.md","content":"## 当前项目\n当前绑定项目：**distill_sparse_swiglu**\n\n## 按需查阅\n- 项目配置：`load_project_config(\"distill_sparse_swiglu\")` 或 `load_project_config(\"distill_sparse_swiglu\", section=\"execution\")`\n- 知识文件：`read_project_file(file=...)` 读取项目文件（ROADMAP.md/memory.md/ideas.md/report.md 等）\n- 路线图：`read_roadmap()` 读取研究方向和短期任务\n- 产出目录：`/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_14/projects/distill_sparse_swiglu/artifacts/`（写文件后用 `register_artifact` 注册）\n\n## 用户自定义规则（必须遵守）\n### 审稿规则\n\n- **[EMNLP 2026]** “EMNLP 2026 通过 ARR 统一审稿，Main/Findings 不分开投稿（不是两个Track），Long/Short 也走同一审稿系统，Overall Assessment的评分标准如下：5 = Consider for Award（约前2.5%），4.5 = Borderline Award，4 = Conference（可被主会议接收），3.5 = Borderline Conference，3 = Findings（可被Findings接收），2.5 = Borderline Findings，2 = Resubmit next cycle（需大幅修改，可在下一周期完成），1.5 = Resubmit after next cycle（需大幅修改，无法在下一周期完成），1 = Do not resubmit（需完全重做或与*ACL无关）”\n\n> 以上规则由用户配置，优先级等同于硬约束。违反会被 Reviewer 标记。\n\n## Worker 操作规范\n\n### paper-writing-norms\n\n# 论文写作风格规范\n\n> 核心哲学：**论文是一个有说服力的故事，不是实验报告。** 审稿人在几十秒内判断论文价值——如果 Abstract 和 Introduction 读起来像实验日志，论文就已经失败了。\n\n---\n\n## 一、总体写作哲学\n\n### 1.1 故事驱动，不是数据堆砌\n\n- 论文必须以\"故事线\"为核心展开：问题 → 洞察 → 方法 → 验证\n- 禁止大量实验数据堆砌——每个数字出现必须服务于叙事推进\n- 附录内容必须在正文中有明确引用且融入叙事，禁止简单堆砌\n- 如果附录数据对核心叙事有重大影响，根据附录数据调整论文 framing\n\n### 1.2 主线统一性\n\n- 当 idea 在研究过程中发生变化后，**必须重审全文逻辑**\n- 常见问题：Introduction 讲的故事 A，Method 做的是故事 B，Results 又在讲故事 C\n- 修复方式：从最终实验结论反推，重写 Introduction 的问题定义和动机\n- 每次 idea 调整后检查：Abstract → Introduction → Method → Results → Discussion → Conclusion 是否形成一条连贯主线\n\n### 1.3 专有名词必须有定义\n\n- 首次出现的专有名词/缩写必须给出完整定义和解释\n- Abstract 中使用的缩写也必须在 Abstract 内定义（如 LLM = Large Language Model）\n- 不能假设读者知道你自己定义的术语——论文从来没解释过的概念不能直接使用\n- 通用规则：如果一个非标准术语第一次出现时没有括号定义，就是写作 bug\n\n### 1.4 写作前必读同类优秀论文","numLines":50,"startLine":0,"totalLines":277}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CBnqdQgwrmiDmS9BvurxVZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read the full paper and the review context. Let me understand the task:\n\n1. I need to dispatch two reviewers (R1: methods+experiments, R2: novelty+related work)\n2. Run a full roundtable (Step 1: independent reviews, Step 2: cross-sharing, Step 3: convergence, Step 4: synthesis)\n3. Submit the final review report\n\nLet me first carefully digest the paper and context, then dispatch both reviewers in parallel.\n\nThe paper is about KL-divergence distillation for training contextual sparsity predictors in SwiGLU-based LLMs. Key claims:\n\n\n1. KL divergence discovers different mask patterns than magnitude-based approaches\n2. At 30% sparsity, BCE loss nearly matches KL performance, suggesting the oracle discovery might not be as novel\n3. The sparsity regime characterization spans 6 points but shows some monotonicity violations\n4. The conceptual contributions include a loss taxonomy and gradient SNR analysis\n\nThe review context flags several critical weaknesses: the C1 ablation shows seed inconsistency (exact match at seed 42 but gaps at seeds 123 and 456), BCE nearly matches KL at the recommended operating point, the regime curve has monotonicity violations, and there are incomplete benchmark results on LongBench and MT-Bench.\n\nRULER results aren't providing meaningful insights. Now I need to set up parallel reviews from two independent reviewers with the full paper, making sure to keep the tier classifications hidden so they can evaluate blindly.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33386,"cache_read_input_tokens":25147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33386},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"263fa585-9870-446a-8635-ded3c7ec2e0a","uuid":"59bc81b3-d076-4a80-8123-0e1b3e0cac85"}
