{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LB95fze4zX4yDV6QqVW3Ho","type":"tool_result","content":"paper/experiments.tex:22:We compare against: (1) \\textbf{Vanilla TEAL}~\\cite{liu2025teal}, which uses activation magnitudes directly; (2) \\textbf{BCE predictor} (DejaVu-style~\\cite{liu2023dejavu}), trained with per-neuron binary cross-entropy on magnitude-based oracle masks for 1000 and 2700 steps; (3) \\textbf{Uniform allocation}, which distributes the sparsity budget equally across layers; and (4) \\textbf{WINA}~\\cite{liu2025teal}, an importance-weighted variant."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018VoMzh2vKwfMRwBjtcVHhW","session_id":"263fa585-9870-446a-8635-ded3c7ec2e0a","uuid":"07f6b22e-a197-4e46-8bea-a06b89fdc5ec","timestamp":"2026-05-18T18:39:27.190Z"}
